#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-decky: Decky Loader for Hearth's Steam Game Mode (docs/STEAM-GAME-MODE.md), as root.

Decky Loader is built into Hearth OS: the image ships a pinned stable release in /usr/lib/hearth-decky (PluginLoader and
its version, os-bases/peppermint/build.sh) and a service template, hearth-decky@.service (User=root, as Decky needs; not
started at boot). nimbus-session starts hearth-decky@<you>.service when Steam Game Mode starts and stops it afterwards,
without a password (49-hearth-decky.rules: only your own instance, only from the active session at the device, only
for administrators). The service runs:

  hearth-decky run USER       get ready, then become Decky Loader: ~USER/homebrew and Steam's CEF remote debugging for
                              USER (Decky needs it), Hearth Sync (/usr/share/hearth/decky-hearth-sync, docs/HEARTH-SYNC.md)
                              and the image's other plugins in PLUGINS (Hearth Link) and ThemeDeck (docs/THEMEDECK.md)
                              brought up to date in Decky's plugins folder, the older Hearth plugin and the retired
                              Hearth Music Hearth put there taken away (your Hearth Music songs carried over to
                              ThemeDeck once), and an install from before (hearth-decky.service and /var/lib/hearth-decky)
                              removed

Older Hearth OS versions downloaded Decky when asked (hearth-admin decky-install, an administrator's password); those
commands stay for images without the built-in one and for clean-up:

  hearth-decky install USER   built in: only the user side and Hearth Sync (nothing downloaded). Otherwise Decky Loader's
                              latest stable release from its GitHub releases into /var/lib/hearth-decky and
                              hearth-decky.service (never started at boot), as before
  hearth-decky remove USER    an install from before: its service, program, Hearth's plugins and the CEF debugging file
                              Hearth made (Decky's settings and other plugins in ~/homebrew stay). Refused for the
                              built-in one (it runs only in Steam Game Mode anyway)
  hearth-decky start|stop     the service of an install from before (the built-in one is started by nimbus-session)

Plugin updates without a system update (docs/PLUGIN-UPDATES.md), as you: plugins-status, plugins-check, plugins-update,
plugins-auto (the daily timer), plugins-builtin, plugins-auto-set on|off, plugins-new-set on|off (see "plugin updates"
below).

A Decky installed with Decky's own installer (plugin_loader.service) is always left alone: it runs by itself, and the
built-in one doesn't start next to it. Prints one JSON line ({"ok": true, ...}); errors print "error: ..." and exit 1.
Paths can be moved for tests with HEARTH_DECKY_ROOT (a folder standing in for /).
"""
